# Line ending policy for Kaiwu
#
# This file locks line endings to match the conventions used in the repo
# at HEAD, so that future contributors don't accidentally introduce the
# LF/CRLF churn that previously caused diff noise (commit 8c85f9f era
# warnings about "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time Git touches it").
#
# Rules:
#   - *.bat          CRLF — required by Windows cmd.exe. Without CRLF, multi-line
#                    for /d blocks and parenthesis-blocks behave unpredictably
#                    on zh-CN Windows (GBK codepage 936).
#   - *.js, *.css, *.html, *.json, *.md  LF — readable in all editors, matches
#                    what `prettier --write` emits under the .prettierrc.json
#                    `"endOfLine": "lf"` setting.
#   - * text=auto    — fallback: Git decides for everything else.

*.bat          text eol=crlf
*.js           text eol=lf
*.css          text eol=lf
*.html         text eol=lf
*.json         text eol=lf
*.md           text eol=lf
*.xml          text eol=lf
*.yml          text eol=lf
*.yaml         text eol=lf

# Let Git decide for everything else
*              text=auto
